Napisane przez: Anna Wr=C3=B3blewska (czwartek, 12 listopada 2026, 22:47)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Dear Students,

Following several questions about the upcoming deadlines and project
requirements, I would like to clarify a few points for all teams.

1. UPCOMING DEADLINES

*
NOVEMBER 18: Mid-term project presentation (SOTA + PoC) =E2=80=94 10-minute=
 team
video.

*
NOVEMBER 25: Mandatory mid-term Q&A session. Prepare substantive questions
about other teams' projects.

*
DECEMBER 2: Phase 2 submission =E2=80=94 revised literature review, EDA, Po=
C,
updated report, source code (Pull Request), and rebuttal.

2. MID-TERM PRESENTATIONS AND TEAMS CHANNEL

A DEDICATED MICROSOFT TEAMS CHANNEL WILL BE CREATED WITHIN THE NEXT FEW
DAYS for submitting and sharing your presentation videos.

You will be able to review other teams' presentations before the November
25 Q&A session, prepare relevant questions, and share them on the channel.

The mid-term video should cover your research problem, SOTA, proposed
methodology, current PoC progress, preliminary findings, and next steps.

THE MID-TERM VIDEO IS NOT GRADED AS A SEPARATE DELIVERABLE, BUT IT IS AN
IMPORTANT PREPARATION MILESTONE FOR THE ASSESSED PHASE 2 PROJECT. Its
content directly relates to several Phase 2 grading criteria: working PoC
(2.1), experimental plan (2.3), and revised state of the art (2.5).

The presentation and Q&A are opportunities to identify weaknesses, receive
feedback, and improve your work before the December 2 submission. Your
responses to the feedback and Q&A questions are also assessed under
Criterion 2.4.

We also have a mandatory Q&A session, which will be much easier for all of
us with the videos beforehand; otherwise, we would have to listen to 20
presentations at once, which is extremely tiring. So we will have only
short videos and a discussion by each team.

THEREFORE, PLEASE TREAT THE MID-TERM PRESENTATION SERIOUSLY, EVEN THOUGH IT
DOES NOT CARRY A SEPARATE SCORE.

3. PHASE 2 REPORT =E2=80=94 TEMPLATES AND LENGTH

You may either extend your Phase 1 report or use the final project report
template, transferring and revising relevant sections. Both approaches are
acceptable.

I recommend APPROXIMATELY 8 PAGES OF MAIN CONTENT, excluding references and
appendices. This is a suggestion, NOT A MANDATORY PAGE LIMIT OR GRADING
CRITERION.

You may place detailed rebuttals, additional experimental results, and
supporting technical information in appendices. However, essential
methodology, results, and conclusions must appear in the main report.

QUALITY, CLARITY, AND COMPLETENESS MATTER MORE THAN THE EXACT NUMBER OF
PAGES.

4. REBUTTAL =E2=80=94 PART OF PHASE 2 ASSESSMENT

CRITERION 2.4: REBUTTAL TO SUPERVISORS' REVIEWS AND Q&A QUESTIONS =E2=80=
=94 3
POINTS.

You are expected to:

*
Address every comment from your supervisors and every question your team
received during Q&A.

*
Explain whether each point was addressed, rejected with justification, or
deferred.

*
Support your arguments with evidence and relevant literature.

*
REVISE YOUR REPORT ACCORDINGLY, clearly indicating where changes were made.

You may initially prepare your rebuttal using the Project Proposal
Template, but the resulting corrections and conclusions must be
incorporated into your Phase 2 report.

Simply acknowledging comments is not sufficient.

5. POC EXPECTATIONS

For November 18, present what you have actually completed. Small-scale
experiments and preliminary results are acceptable if their limitations are
clearly explained.

For the graded Phase 2 submission on December 2, Criterion 2.1 requires a
working, reproducible PoC producing measurable results on real data.

6. SURVEY PRESENTATIONS AND TUTORIALS

The SURVEY PRESENTATION/TUTORIAL (CRITERION 5C, 10 POINTS) is a separate
requirement and has not been replaced by the mid-term project video.

It involves presenting an NLP research topic grounded in relevant
scientific literature, along with the required quiz and demonstration
notebook.

Please consult the course schedule for the December presentation sessions.

7. SCIENTIFIC REASONING AND PROFESSIONAL DATA SCIENCE

Evidence-based reasoning, methodological rigour, reproducibility,
professional communication, and critical collaboration with AI are
important LEARNING OUTCOMES OF THIS MASTER'S-LEVEL COURSE.

The rebuttal process is not simply an opportunity to negotiate grades. It
is an exercise in evaluating evidence, defending methodological decisions,
responding constructively to criticism, and improving your work.

I am happy to reconsider scores when convincing evidence demonstrates an
assessment error. However, ALL CORRECTIONS MUST BE VERIFIED AND APPLIED
CONSISTENTLY AND FAIRLY ACROSS TEAMS.

Finally, TUTORIAL ATTENDANCE IS MANDATORY. Please reread the published
course rules and grading criteria, as well as our university rules.

Thank you for your engagement and constructive discussions!

Best regards,
Anna Wr=C3=B3blewska

